<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-19520] FLR-EC: Don't read parity components on old clients</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19520</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;We need to make sure that older clients do not try to read the parity components. This can probably be handled by setting the layout pattern of the parity components to &lt;tt&gt;LOV_PATTERN_PARITY&lt;/tt&gt;, but this needs to be tested.  It may be desirable to exclude the &lt;tt&gt;LOV_PATTERN_PARITY&lt;/tt&gt; components from the layout that is sent to older clients, since 2.15.x does not (yet) have patch &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/51060" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/51060&lt;/a&gt; ("&lt;tt&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16837" title="interop: client skip unknown component mirror" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16837"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-16837&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; llite: handle unknown layout component&lt;/tt&gt;") to handle FLR-EC layouts properly.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
